Avoid state corruption via bailout -- UNOFFICIAL analogy backport to PHP 5.5.38

Backport by analogy (NOT a direct diff application) of the PHP security team's
"Avoid state corruption via bailout" fix to the EOL 5.5 branch, which received
no official patch. 5.5 uses the OLD Zend engine (old zend_mm allocator, old
HashTable, TSRMLS_* threading), so the changes are adapted to 5.x idioms while
keeping the defensive intent identical.

  Fix GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w (CVE-2026-109618)  -- OOM/overflow no longer longjmp()s
  Fix GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp (CVE-2026-109619)  -- stale request-owned global state

zend_mm_safe_error_ex() is exported (ZEND_API) so the Zend/zend_strtod.c Balloc()
allocation-failure site is covered too, for parity with the 5.4 sibling port.

Reference: upstream commit 712e60f9edfd03f0960fc4fc3c2c375f42b90aa2 (7.x).
Applies to a pristine php-5.5.38 tree with: patch -p1 --forward --batch
